{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/574931-suggestions-on-what-to-read","id":574931,"title":"Suggestions on what to read","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-01T02:48:27-07:00","id":574931,"title":"Suggestions on what to read","content":"Just looking for some ideas on a good series to start reading. I've always been a fan of the World of Darkness, and have read nearly all of their novels and am looking for anything of a similar type. (Yeah, I've read most of Shadowrun as well). I guess I'm probably looking for newer series, I've read a lot of older ones (or skipped them for whatever reason), but I haven't really kept up with any new series in the last ten years or so. Anything Cthulhu Mythos (or Things Man Was Not Meant to Know), World of Darkness-y, Warhammer 40k-ish, Star Wars-like, or anything else that's new (relatively) and exciting. I guess I like intrigue, secret Cosmic Forces, and action. I have looked up various lists and suggestions, but I felt that anyone who answers me on this forum will probably have a good idea of what I'm asking for. Thanks to anyone who helps me out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6688-tungee","name":"tungee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T05:58:14-07:00","id":575100,"title":"","content":"One go to that I can recommend to pretty much anyone that likes WoD type games is <i>The Dresden Files</i> by Jim Butcher. It's a very popular urban fantasy series. It is my favorite series. When you get past that, it really comes down to a statement of &quot;we need more details&quot;. There are lots of other books that I could possibly recommend, but I would need to know more about your tastes. Do you like YA fiction, for example?<br /> <br /> One series that I quite like and would recommend is the <i>Kara Gillian</i> series written by Diana Rowland which starts with a book titled <i>Mark of the Demon</i>. It's about a detective in Louisiana, USA who summons demons in order to help her with her work and also just because it's fucking awesome. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I would like more details of your preferences before I can really make any solid recommendations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T07:00:01-07:00","id":575166,"title":"","content":"I second Jim Butcher's <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Storm-Front-Dresden-Files-Butcher/dp/0451457811/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1435759055&amp;sr=8-1&amp;keywords=jim+butcher+dresden+files\" target=\"_blank\">The Dresden Files</a>. <br /> <br /> Neil Gaiman's <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/American-Gods-Neil-Gaiman/dp/0380789035/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1435759082&amp;sr=8-1&amp;keywords=american+gods+neil+gaiman\" target=\"_blank\">American Gods</a> and <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Neverwhere-A-Novel-Neil-Gaiman/dp/0060557818/ref=pd_sim_14_1?ie=UTF8&amp;refRID=16VEFNM42M9EA4RV33QA\" target=\"_blank\">Neverwhere</a> also have a vibe similar to WoD.<br /> <br /> For a more Cthulhu vibe, try Jeff Vandermeer's Southern Reach Trilogy (<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Annihilation-Novel-Southern-Reach-Trilogy/dp/0374104093/ref=sr_1_1?s=books&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1435759124&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=southern+reach+trilogy\" target=\"_blank\">Annihilation</a>, <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Authority-Novel-Southern-Reach-Trilogy/dp/0374104107/ref=pd_bxgy_14_img_y\" target=\"_blank\">Authority</a>, and <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Acceptance-Novel-Southern-Reach-Trilogy/dp/0374104115/ref=pd_bxgy_14_img_y\" target=\"_blank\">Acceptance</a>). They aren't actually Lovecraft, but have that same horrors from the other world feeling.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T07:14:31-07:00","id":575179,"title":"","content":"Laurell K Hamilton is also a good author. I know, she has her faults, but she does pretty great with world building. Her main series is Anita Blake and it is about a world wherein vampires and werewolves are considered legal citizens. Her other series, Merry Gentry, is about a fae in the modern world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T07:31:02-07:00","id":575188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/574931-suggestions-on-what-to-read?p=575179#post575179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Laurell K Hamilton is also a good author. I know, she has her faults, but she does pretty great with world building. Her main series is Anita Blake and it is about a world wherein vampires and werewolves are considered legal citizens. Her other series, Merry Gentry, is about a fae in the modern world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Her first three Merry Gentry books were awesome. After that, not so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T10:14:38-07:00","id":575330,"title":"","content":"Charles Stross' Laundry Files. Starts with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Atrocity_Archives\" target=\"_blank\">The Atrocity Archives</a>.<br /> <br /> I've been really enjoying Brian P. Easton's <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Autobiography-Werewolf-Hunter-Brian-Easton/dp/1934861294\" target=\"_blank\">Autobiography of a Werewolf Hunter</a> trilogy, which ended recently. It's sort of Punisher meets Bale Hounds. My wife just got into it too, halfway through the second book and loving it too.<br /> <br /> And while it's not a series, Laird Barron's <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Light-Darkness-Laird-Barron-ebook/dp/B008RDKN7W/\" target=\"_blank\">The Light Is The Darkness</a> is just an awesome book that fits some of the things you wanted. The author's written a number of great anthologies that I recommend as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-01-2015, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T17:21:14-07:00","id":575795,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your advice. Some of them I have read before (Neil Gaiman's work), and others I've avoided for various reasons (The Dresden Files, but in my defense my first experience with them was the television show and then sort of turned me off, although I realize they are very different. Enough people have recommended them to me that maybe I should give it a shot). I'm going to look up the rest of these and pick from among them.<br /> <br /> Preferences: I guess dark, high fantasy. I also like the stories that have a Lovecraftian feel (where we, humans, are basically small deluded things adrift in an uncaring cosmos filled with vast horrors beyond comprehension), but I do prefer more action than simply psychological horror (although I definitely don't mind it when it appears in the works I do like). I'm assuming &quot;YA&quot; means &quot;young adult&quot; and, if so, then no, I am not a fan. I'm not interested much in romance or any sex (honestly, I would prefer to never see either of them at all, but occasionally I find something that I do like (although I've never found one -based- on those concepts that I was fond of. If romance shows up during the course of the story, fine, but I never look for it. I don't generally care who the main character is (man, woman, wizard, warrior, etc) so long as their main goal isn't getting laid or finding love (there's a pattern here). I'm former Army Special Ops, so anything then delves into modern (relatively) warfare I at least like to make logical sense (no groups of baddies encircling a group of people and then firing, essentially indiscriminately, at their buddies on the other side of the circle).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6688-tungee","name":"tungee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T06:36:10-07:00","id":576305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tungee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/574931-suggestions-on-what-to-read?p=575795#post575795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Others I've avoided for various reasons (The Dresden Files, but in my defense my first experience with them was the television show and then sort of turned me off, although I realize they are very different. Enough people have recommended them to me that maybe I should give it a shot). I'm going to look up the rest of these and pick from among them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am a big fan of the Dresden Files books, but did not like the TV show. The series gets really good starting on Book 3. The TV show is more like books 1 and 2. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tungee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/574931-suggestions-on-what-to-read?p=575795#post575795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Preferences: I guess dark, high fantasy. I also like the stories that have a Lovecraftian feel (where we, humans, are basically small deluded things adrift in an uncaring cosmos filled with vast horrors beyond comprehension)</div> </div> </div> </div>I highly suggest the Southern Reach series then. It is very much &quot;Humans are small deluded things adrift in an uncaring cosmos.&quot; Here is the <a href=\"http://io9.com/read-the-mesmerizing-first-chapter-of-jeff-vandermeers-1520682658\" target=\"_blank\">first chapter of the first book</a>. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:02:23-07:00","id":586308,"title":"","content":"I want to second the Laundry Files books, I am halfway through the the most recent one (The Annihilation Score) and it is some of the best urban fantasy ever, the mixing of the Cthulhu mythos with modern geek culture and computer science is a brilliant one and the characters hit a great level of scary and funny, the humor is great and works as a great counterpoint for some seriously dark shit. <br /> <br /> Read them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}